  "notes": "Source: Elmhurst University official 'Baccalaureate Program Student Handbook 2025-2026' (Department of Nursing and Public Health), APPENDIX A: Pre-licensure (Traditional BSN) Plan of Study, hand-transcribed 2026-10-02 from the official handbook PDF. Course titles cross-checked against the official NRS Major Evaluation Form (2024-25 catalog, elmhurst.edu). Elmhurst uses course credits: 1.00 course credit = 4 semester hours; credits below are converted to semester hours (.75=3, .50=2, 1.25=5). Published term totals verified: Fall Y1 4.0/16, Spring Y1 4.0/16, Fall Y2 4.0/16, Spring Y2 4.0/16, Fall Y3 4.0/16, Spring Y3 3.75/15, Fall Y4 3.5/14, Spring Y4 3.5/14; plan total 30.75 course credits / 123 semester hours. The plan's three '(EIC) (1)' slots (one Fall Y2, two Spring Y2) are Elmhurst Integrated Curriculum Area-of-Knowledge electives, modeled as choice slots; together with the named courses they reconcile the published Year 2 total of 8.0/32. Grade rules from the plan: a grade of C or higher is required in all nursing and natural-science prerequisite courses (BIO 107, BIO 108, BIO 221, CHM 101, CHM 103, PSY 210, PSY 315, PSY 327, MTH and Statistics). The plan notes an Advanced Chemistry option (CHM 123 Gen/Organic/Biochem, 1.25 credits) may replace CHM 101/CHM 103 for eligible students; the standard CHM 101 + CHM 103 path is modeled here to match the published totals. The plan's J-Term row carries no courses. Elmhurst requires 32 course credits (128 semester hours) for the bachelor's degree; the published plan totals 30.75/123 and the plan itself directs students to add EIC coursework ('+1 EIC') toward the degree total. No course-to-course prerequisites are stated in the plan of study, so prereq lists are empty.",
